# Athletic Genome lives in its own repo and its own Netlify site, because a
# Python engine generates its data and that pipeline should not be forked.
# Serve it here under /genome anyway: Netlify fetches the page from the other
# site and returns it as if it were ours (status 200 = rewrite, not redirect),
# so the URL bar stays on ndmlabs.net. That site is built with Astro
# base '/genome', so all its links and assets already carry the prefix and
# come back through this same rule.
/genome/*  https://athletic-genome.netlify.app/genome/:splat  200

# Bare /genome has no splat to match; send it to the mounted root.
/genome  /genome/  301
